Source: sg-shell
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), gcc-mingw-w64-x86-64, gcc-mingw-w64-i686, python3, python3-numpy, python3-pil, python3-fonttools, fonts-inter, unicode-data
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Homepage: https://github.com/Stained-Glass-OS/sg-shell
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: sg-shell
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, wine-sg | wine, fonts-inter, fonts-liberation,
         fonts-crosextra-carlito, fonts-crosextra-caladea, fonts-cascadia-code,
         fonts-noto-cjk,
         python3, sg-session (>= 0.1.0-91), xterm, libglib2.0-bin,
         librsvg2-bin
Description: Stained Glass OS shell panels (Start menu, Control Panel, Task Manager)
 Windows 10-style panels for the surfaces Wine's explorer does not provide:
 the Start menu (sg-start), the Control Panel (sg-control), Remote Desktop
 Connection (sg-mstsc) and gpresult. The taskbar's appearance is handled in
 wine-sg, not here. Panels install as PE programs under
 /usr/libexec/stained-glass/shell.
 .
 The Control Panel's administrative changes (computer name, domain, local
 accounts, time zone, update checks) are made by sg-admind, a root service
 that acts only on requests from the elevated SYSTEM account.

Package: sg-office
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, sg-shell (= ${source:Version}), wine-sg | wine, sg-office-editors
Description: SG Office for Stained Glass OS (documents, spreadsheets, presentations)
 The office suite's place in Stained Glass OS: SG Office Documents,
 Spreadsheets and Presentations in the Start menu, the default programs for
 Microsoft Office's file types (until the user installs another suite) and
 Settings > Default apps rows. They start SG Office's editors, our own suite
 based on ONLYOFFICE (package sg-office-editors).
